To change the sentiment of the sentence, you can use a sentiment transfer tool that allows you to input a sentence and specify the target sentiment. Then, the tool will convert the original sentiment to the target sentiment while keeping the rest of the content unchanged. Here's an example of how to do this using the sentiment transfer tool on Google Docs:

1. Open Google Docs and create a new document.
2. Type the original sentence in the document.
3. Click on the ""Sentiment"" dropdown menu on the top left corner of the page.
4. Select ""Positive"" from the dropdown menu.
5. Click on the ""Convert"" button on the top right corner of the page.
6. In the next dialog box, specify the target sentiment as ""Negative"".
7. Click on the ""Convert"" button again.
8. The sentence will now have the negative sentiment.

Note: The sentiment transfer tool may not always produce accurate results, so it's important to test it on a small sample of sentences to ensure its accuracy."
